course: dictionary
lesson: 3670
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «She was given a fitting end to the story.» Here fitting means right and suitable, not a size or a shape.
explain: «kělè («KUH-luh») is cola, a loanword; the kě sounds like the word for thirsty, which makes it a fitting name.» Fitting means suitable, so the name is right for the drink. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Fitting can also be a noun. «A dress fitting» is a time when you try on clothes so they can be made the right size, and «bathroom fittings» are the small parts fixed to a room, like taps and light switches. Look at the words beside fitting to find its meaning.
fact: Fitting means right or suitable for a certain time or situation.
fact: «A fitting end» means an ending that feels right and fair.
fact: A fitting is a small part fixed to something, like a tap, a handle or a light.
fact: A fitting can also be a time when you try on clothes so they can be made the right size.
fact: Fit is a verb, and fitting is its -ing form: «The jigsaw piece is fitting nicely» means it is going into place correctly.
exercise: «She was given a fitting end to the story.» Here fitting means: | Lost | Very fast | *Right and suitable | Wet and cold
exercise: Mia goes to a fitting for her school costume. What is a fitting here? | A type of tap | A race | *A time to try on clothes so they are the right size | A kind of cloth
exercise: What does «bathroom fittings» mean? | Water running down the drain | The bath towels | The people who clean the bath | *Small parts fixed to a room, like taps or light switches
test: In «it is fitting that…», fitting means: | *Right or suitable | Very late | Too tight
test: Which sentence uses fitting as the -ing form of fit? | Bathroom fittings are shiny | A dress fitting is next Tuesday | *The jigsaw piece is fitting nicely
exam: In «kělè («KUH-luh») is cola, a loanword; the kě sounds like the word for thirsty, which makes it a fitting name.», what does fitting mean? | *Right and suitable | Cold and wet | A time to try clothes on | A small part fixed to a wall
